# Normalize every text file to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# core.autocrlf is a per-developer setting, so without this file the line
# endings that reach a commit depend on whoever authored it. A contributor
# working on Windows with autocrlf=false would commit CRLF, and the POSIX
# drivers are executed directly on macOS and Linux:
#
#   ./scripts/test.sh
#   ./scripts/differential_test.py
#   ./scripts/benchmark.py
#
# A CRLF shebang fails there with "bad interpreter", so pin the encoding
# rather than relying on every clone being configured the same way.
* text=auto eol=lf
